            <ArticleTitle>Pseudoaneurysm rupture after acute Type A dissection repair: possible reaction to BioGlue.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/icvts/ivx331</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 45-year-old man with acute Type A aortic dissection underwent the ascending aorta replacement with BioGlue (CryoLife Europa, Guildford, Surrey, UK) for anastomotic reinforcement. Postoperatively, he developed descending aortic dilation, a giant mediastinal cyst, Henoch-Schonlein purpura and an anastomotic-site pseudoaneurysm rupture. A BioGlue-induced inflammatory reaction was likely, according to a positive patch test (delayed allergic reaction).</AbstractText>
